Got it! If you're looking to maintain Python environments or local AI toolchains as well, here are quick references for keeping those up to date:
Python Packages (pip)
To list outdated packages and update specific ones:
python3 -m pip list --outdated
python3 -m pip install --upgrade <package_name>

To update all installed pip packages at once:
python3 -m pip list --outdated --format=freeze | grep -v '^\-e' | cut -d = -f 1 | xargs -n1 python3 -m pip install -U

Git Repositories
To sync a local repo with upstream changes:
git fetch origin && git pull --rebase

